  "scope": "A coupled replacement of solo-protection tickets by a newly feasible joint route preserves P and R on each actual ticket, adds Q protection, conserves total tickets, and preserves any previously satisfied individual chance floors. Positive exact-equality lotteries omit the joint route and admit this improvement. A separate diagnostic shows that an available but unselected strongest rescue route changes the specified global filter selection and silences a weaker group. Permission, efficacy, burdens, justified floors, severity and normative force are not derived. Existing aggregation-cycle/composition results are reused, not reproved; no expected-welfare or complete ethical choice rule is established.",
